## Recovery Windows and Retention

### 1. Cold Storage Lifecycle

**Backup Retention Tiers:**
```
Warm Storage (Immediately Accessible)
├─ Available for rapid recovery
├─ Higher cost: ~$0.05/GB for RDS, ~$0.023/GB for EBS
└─ Used for: Recent backups, frequent access

Cold Storage (Archived)
├─ Available but slower access (hours)
├─ Lower cost: ~$0.01/GB for RDS, ~$0.004/GB for EBS
└─ Used for: Long-term retention, compliance, archival

Lifecycle Example:
Day 1-7:   Warm Storage (frequently accessed)
Day 8-30:  Cold Storage (compliance retention)
Day 31:    Deleted
```

### 2. Recovery Point Lifecycle Configuration

```bash
# Create plan with cold storage transition
aws backup create-backup-plan \
  --backup-plan '{
    "BackupPlanName": "LongTermRetention",
    "Rules": [
      {
        "RuleName": "MonthlyBackup",
        "TargetBackupVaultName": "archive-vault",
        "ScheduleExpression": "cron(0 3 1 * ? *)",
        "Lifecycle": {
          "DeleteAfterDays": 2555,
          "MoveToColdStorageAfterDays": 30
        }
      }
    ]
  }'

# Archive policy: Move to cold storage immediately after backup
Lifecycle:
  DeleteAfterDays: 365
  MoveToColdStorageAfterDays: 0  # Immediately cold
```

### 3. Point-in-Time Recovery (PITR)

```bash
# For RDS with PITR enabled
aws backup describe-backup-vault \
  --backup-vault-name prod-vault

# Restore RDS to specific point in time
aws backup start-restore-job \
  --recovery-point-arn arn:aws:backup:us-east-1:123456789012:recovery-point:rds-db-abc123 \
  --iam-role-arn arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/AWSBackupRole \
  --metadata '{
    "availabilityZone": "us-east-1a",
    "port": "3306"
  }'

# PITR Window: RDS default 7 days, configurable up to 35 days
```

