## Backup Vaults

### 1. Create Backup Vault

```bash
# Create standard backup vault
aws backup create-backup-vault \
  --backup-vault-name production-vault \
  --encryption-key-arn arn:aws:kms:us-east-1:123456789012:key/12345678-1234-1234-1234-123456789012 \
  --tags VaultName=ProductionVault,Environment=Prod

# Create vault with access policy
aws backup put-backup-vault-access-policy \
  --backup-vault-name production-vault \
  --policy '{
    "Version": "2012-10-17",
    "Statement": [
      {
        "Effect": "Allow",
        "Principal": {
          "AWS": "arn:aws:iam::123456789012:root"
        },
        "Action": "backup:*",
        "Resource": "*"
      }
    ]
  }'

# Create vault with Backup Lock
aws create-backup-vault-with-backup-lock \
  --backup-vault-name compliance-vault \
  --backup-lock-mode COMPLIANCE \
  --backup-lock-day-count 2555  # 7 years for compliance
```

### 2. Vault Encryption

```bash
# All vaults encrypted by default (AWS-managed key)
# Use customer-managed key for additional control

# Create with custom KMS key
aws backup create-backup-vault \
  --backup-vault-name encrypted-vault \
  --encryption-key-arn arn:aws:kms:us-east-1:123456789012:key/xxxxxxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxx-xxxxxxxxxxxx

# Encryption benefits:
# - Data encrypted at rest
# - Only authorized users can decrypt
# - Audit trail of access
```

### 3. List and Manage Vaults

```bash
# List all backup vaults
aws backup list-backup-vaults

# Describe specific vault
aws backup describe-backup-vault \
  --backup-vault-name production-vault

# List recovery points in vault
aws backup list-recovery-points-by-backup-vault \
  --backup-vault-name production-vault \
  --by-resource-type RDS

# Delete recovery point
aws backup delete-recovery-point \
  --backup-vault-name production-vault \
  --recovery-point-arn arn:aws:backup:us-east-1:123456789012:recovery-point:rds-db-abc123
```

