## Compliance and Management

### 1. Backup Lock (WORM Compliance)

```bash
# Enable Compliance Mode Lock (cannot be modified after 7 days)
aws put-backup-vault-lock-configuration \
  --backup-vault-name compliance-vault \
  --min-retention-days 2555 \
  --max-retention-days 2555 \
  --changeable-for-days 7

# Parameters:
# min-retention-days: Minimum retention (cannot delete before)
# max-retention-days: Maximum retention (cannot keep longer)
# changeable-for-days: Grace period before lock takes effect

# Enable Governance Mode Lock (can override with permissions)
aws put-backup-vault-lock-configuration \
  --backup-vault-name standard-vault \
  --min-retention-days 30 \
  --max-retention-days 365 \
  --changeable-for-days 7

# Verify lock configuration
aws get-backup-vault-lock-configuration \
  --backup-vault-name compliance-vault

# Lock details:
# CreationDate: When lock created
# LockedDate: When lock becomes active
# LockState: COMPLIANCE or GOVERNANCE
```

### 2. Audit and Compliance Reporting

```bash
# List all backup jobs (audit trail)
aws backup list-backup-jobs \
  --by-state COMPLETED \
  --query 'BackupJobs[*].[BackupJobId,ResourceArn,State,CreationDate,CompletionDate]' \
  --output table

# List copy jobs (cross-region backups)
aws backup list-copy-jobs \
  --by-state COMPLETED \
  --query 'CopyJobs[*].[CopyJobId,SourceRecoveryPointArn,Status,CreationDate]' \
  --output table

# List backup plans
aws backup list-backup-plans \
  --query 'BackupPlansList[*].[BackupPlanName,BackupPlanId,CreationDate,LastExecutionDate]' \
  --output table

# Export compliance report
aws backup describe-backup-vault \
  --backup-vault-name compliance-vault \
  --query 'BackupVaultArn' \
  --output text
```

### 3. Backup Compliance Dashboard

```bash
# Get backup statistics
aws backup describe-backup-vault \
  --backup-vault-name production-vault

# Get recovery point statistics
aws backup list-recovery-points-by-backup-vault \
  --backup-vault-name production-vault \
  --query 'RecoveryPoints[*].[RecoveryPointArn,Status,CreationDate]' \
  --output json

# Calculate backup coverage
TOTAL_DBS=$(aws rds describe-db-instances \
  --query 'DBInstances[].DBInstanceIdentifier' \
  --output text | wc -w)

BACKED_UP_DBS=$(aws backup list-recovery-points-by-resource-type \
  --resource-type RDS \
  --query 'RecoveryPoints[].ResourceArn' \
  --output text | sort -u | wc -w)

echo "Database Backup Coverage: $BACKED_UP_DBS / $TOTAL_DBS"
```

