## Best Practices

### 1. Backup Planning Strategy

```bash
# Define RPO/RTO requirements
# RPO (Recovery Point Objective): How much data loss acceptable?
# RTO (Recovery Time Objective): How quickly must system recover?

# Example RPO/RTO matrix:
# Critical: RPO=1hr, RTO=15min → Hourly backups, fast restoration
# Important: RPO=4hr, RTO=1hr → 4x daily backups, standard restoration
# Non-critical: RPO=24hr, RTO=8hr → Daily backups, slower restoration
```

### 2. Retention Policy

```bash
# Hot storage: 7 days (warm, immediate access)
# Cold storage: 30 days (archived, slower access)
# Delete: After 365 days (or compliance requirement)

# Calculate backup storage cost
# Example: 100 GB database
# Daily backups for 30 days: 3 TB × $0.05 = $150/month
# Move to cold after 7 days: 3 TB × $0.01 = $30/month
# Total savings with cold storage: ~60%
```

### 3. Tagging Strategy

```bash
# Tag backups for organization and cost allocation
RecoveryPointTags:
  {
    "BackupType": "Daily|Weekly|Monthly",
    "Environment": "Production|Development|Testing",
    "CostCenter": "Engineering|Finance",
    "Application": "AppName",
    "ComplianceRequired": "true|false"
  }
```

### 4. Testing Restore Procedures

```bash
# Schedule monthly restore tests
# Monthly: Restore one random backup to test environment
# Verify: Data integrity, application functionality
# Document: Recovery time, success/failure details

# Create automated restore test
aws backup start-restore-job \
  --recovery-point-arn <random-recovery-point-arn> \
  --iam-role-arn arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/AWSBackupRole \
  --metadata '{
    "DBInstanceIdentifier": "test-restore-$(date +%Y%m%d-%H%M%S)"
  }'
```

### 5. Monitoring and Alerts

```bash
# Set CloudWatch alarms for backup failures
aws cloudwatch put-metric-alarm \
  --alarm-name backup-job-failed \
  --alarm-description "Alert on backup job failure" \
  --metric-name BackupJobsFailed \
  --namespace AWS/Backup \
  --statistic Sum \
  --threshold 1 \
  --comparison-operator GreaterThanOrEqualToThreshold \
  --alarm-actions arn:aws:sns:us-east-1:123456789012:backup-alerts

# Monitor backup completion time
aws cloudwatch put-metric-alarm \
  --alarm-name backup-job-duration \
  --metric-name BackupJobDuration \
  --namespace AWS/Backup \
  --statistic Average \
  --threshold 3600000  # milliseconds (1 hour)
  --comparison-operator GreaterThanThreshold
```

### 6. Cross-Account Strategy

```bash
# Centralized backup account architecture:
# - Central account: Stores all backups from multiple accounts
# - Backup accounts: Run backup plans, copy to central
# - Benefits: Centralized management, cross-account recovery, cost allocation
```

