## Troubleshooting

### Problem 1: Backup Job Failed

**Error:** `BackupJobFailedException`

**Solution:**
```bash
# Get job details
aws backup describe-backup-job \
  --backup-job-id backup-job-12345678

# Common causes:
# 1. IAM role missing permissions
# 2. Resource doesn't support backup
# 3. Network/connectivity issues
# 4. Insufficient storage space

# Add required IAM permissions
aws iam attach-role-policy \
  --role-name AWSBackupRole \
  --policy-arn arn:aws:iam::aws:policy/AWSBackupServiceRolePolicyForBackup
```

### Problem 2: Restore Fails

**Error:** `RestoreJobFailedException`

**Solution:**
```bash
# Verify recovery point exists
aws backup describe-recovery-point \
  --backup-vault-name prod-vault \
  --recovery-point-arn arn:aws:backup:...

# Check target resource compatibility
# Verify IAM role has restore permissions
# Verify network connectivity

# Retry restore with explicit parameters
aws backup start-restore-job \
  --recovery-point-arn arn:aws:backup:... \
  --iam-role-arn arn:aws:iam::123456789012:role/AWSBackupRole \
  --metadata '{"DBInstanceIdentifier": "restored-db"}'
```

### Problem 3: Cross-Region Copy Failing

**Error:** `CrossRegionCopyFailedException`

**Solution:**
```bash
# Verify destination vault exists in target region
aws backup describe-backup-vault \
  --backup-vault-name dr-vault \
  --region us-west-2

# Check IAM permissions for cross-region copy
# Verify KMS key accessible in both regions
# Check network connectivity between regions

# Re-enable copy action
aws backup update-backup-plan \
  --backup-plan-id plan-id \
  --backup-plan file://updated-plan.json
```

### Problem 4: Vault Lock Cannot Be Modified

**Error:** `BackupVaultLocked`

**Solution:**
```bash
# Check lock status
aws get-backup-vault-lock-configuration \
  --backup-vault-name compliance-vault

# If in grace period: Wait until changeable-for-days expires
# If compliance mode: Cannot modify (permanent)
# If governance mode: Can be overridden by authorized users

# Override governance lock (if authorized)
aws put-backup-vault-access-policy \
  --backup-vault-name vault-name \
  --policy file://new-policy.json
```

